# Data Layer

## DTO vs domain

| Layer | Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Remote DTO | `core/data/api/{topic}/models/*Dto.kt` and Apollo-generated classes under `core/graphql/` | Wire format (GraphQL responses, Supabase storage payloads) |
| Domain model | `features/{feature}/domain/models/` | Domain shape consumed by features |

Rules:
- Apollo-generated types live in `dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.graphql.*` and are treated as DTOs. They never leak past the repository.
- Hand-written DTOs live under `core/data/...` with the `Dto` suffix and are `internal` (only the data layer touches them).
- Domain models live next to their consumer (`features/<feature>/domain/models/`) without the `Dto` suffix.
- DTO→domain mapping is the **repository's** responsibility, not a separate UseCase. The repository is the boundary; everything outside the repository sees domain types.

## Repository contract

Repositories expose `suspend fun (): Result<T>` (one-shot). No Flow boilerplate unless a feature truly observes a live stream.

Errors surface as `Result.failure(throwable)` via the `coRunCatching { ... }` helper from `common/extensions/CoroutineExtensions.kt`. Loading is tracked as a `Store.State.isLoading: Boolean` flag, not a Result variant. See `mobile-error-handling.mdc`.

## Dispatchers

`CoroutineDispatchers` is injected (interface in `common/coroutines/CoroutineDispatchers.kt`). Never reference `Dispatchers.IO` / `Dispatchers.Default` directly from `commonMain` — go through the abstraction so tests can substitute `UnconfinedTestDispatcher`.

Note: on Kotlin/Native, `Dispatchers.IO` is exposed via an extension property — `common/coroutines/Dispatchers.kt` has a load-bearing `import kotlinx.coroutines.IO` guarded by `@file:Suppress("UnusedImport")`. Do not remove it.

## Mappers

Mappers live next to the data they convert. For Apollo → domain conversion: `core/data/api/{topic}/mappers/{Topic}Mappers.kt`. For other conversions, prefer extension functions colocated with the target type.

Style: free-standing `internal fun ApolloType.toDomain(): DomainType = ...`. UI-state mappers (Store `State`/`Label` → `Ui*State`/`Ui*Label`) live under `features/<feature>/presentation/mappers/` as `Api` + `internal class Impl`, bound through `<feature>/impl/di/<Feature>ImplModule.kt` with `singleOf(::Impl) bind Api::class`.

## Repository Cache

`ResourcesRepository` (`core/data/repository/resources/`) aggregates remote and local sources and caches them in memory.

Rules:
- Cache keys live inside the repository as private constants.
- No TTL today. If you add one, document it in the repository file and surface it in the constructor (e.g., `ttl: Duration = 1.hours`).
- Repositories never throw to the caller; wrap exceptions via `coRunCatching { ... }` so they emerge as `Result.failure(throwable)`. Log in the catch block with `Napier.e(throwable = ..., message = ...)`.

## Local JSON Constants

`shared/common-resources/src/commonMain/moko-resources/files/constant_{heroes,items,abilities}.json` ships with the app. `:shared:core-resources/.../data/local/constants/ConstantResourcesDataSource` reads them through the `FileContentReader` expect/actual (Android needs `Context`, JVM/iOS do not) and deserializes with `kotlinx.serialization`. These models (`Hero`, `Item`, `Ability`) are domain entities, not DTOs — they are consumed as-is by features.
